{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question","id":463783,"title":"Crossover Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-31T13:20:01-07:00","id":463783,"title":"Crossover Question","content":"If I recall correctly, in VtR 1e, other supernaturals such as mages and werewolves were immune to the Vinculum and Embrace, but could still suffer from vitae addiction.<br /> <br /> I did not see any mention of this in VtR 2e. Have there been any official crossover rules promulgated for 2e, and has this issue ever been addressed. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:26:36-07:00","id":463824,"title":"","content":"It has! And the answer is, in fact, in the FAQ.<br /> <br /> Other supernaturals can become blood bond and vitae-addicted. The only question left is whether they can be Embraced, but this probably defaults to &quot;no&quot;, like all template-mixing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:37:55-07:00","id":463835,"title":"","content":"And likewise, they can't be ghouled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:45:01-07:00","id":464935,"title":"","content":"I have let other things be embraced, but I just have the beast kill whatever it was before. Like the changeling would lose whatever fae abilities they had, I dont think I would let a demon be embraced because they werent really human to begin with so when the demon part dies... there isnt really anything left. If that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T14:49:22-07:00","id":466539,"title":"","content":"Well, demons, prometheans and werewolves aren't human, so that's a no-go. Mummies are already walking corpses, and a sin-eater will just get back up. That just leaves changelings and mages. I'm not sure changelings have enough soul left to form the Man and something is <i>bound</i> to go funny with mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T08:30:15-07:00","id":467418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=466539#post466539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolves aren't human,</div> </div> </div> </div> Nitpick - werewolves <i>claim</i> to not be human. They're not on the same level of not-human as the Created and Unchained are. The latter two are more akin to self-aware robots, while the former was born of humans and spent much of its life as a human before the Change.<br /> <br /> Mages claim to still be human, but, from a metagame stand point, they're &quot;Mental Monsters.&quot; I think its the same thing with werewolf, just in reverse. I see no reason for werewolves to be that different of a consideration from a changeling in this case. Especially given the wide variety of answers to the question of &quot;what happens when a vampire embraces a werewolf&quot; in popular culture. <br /> <br /> So, saying werewolves are automatically a no-go is kinda harsh, especially to me, since my personal pet theory is that vampires all originated as cannibalistic versions of other supernaturals. The prometheans that stole vitrol, human eating wolves, soul-stealing mages, shadow-eating fetches, and hungry ghosts all manage to thrive, but started to feed on each other. Over time, the whole &quot;you are what you eat&quot; rule came into play, and became more and more like each other, until we got the modern day vampires.<br /> <br /> So, Tremere, to me, aren't just vampire-like. They're beings who've started on the path to evolving into actual vampires. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-03-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T08:49:03-07:00","id":467426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=467418#post467418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nitpick - werewolves <i>claim</i> to not be human. They're not on the same level of not-human as the Created and Unchained are. The latter two are more akin to self-aware robots, while the former was born of humans and spent much of its life as a human before the Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book seems to support the idea that they are not human.<br /> <br /> From the Legends &amp; Lies section:<br /> 'Werewolves are people who change into wolves.<br /> No. We were born and raised looking like humans, but that is a disguise. We don\u2019t have one true form, we have five \u2014 each of which has a purpose in the hunt.'<br /> <br /> Also the first line in Chapter 2, 'Werewolves aren't human.' Along with other mentions of them not being human scattered throughout the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:06:41-07:00","id":467856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=467418#post467418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nitpick - werewolves <i>claim</i> to not be human. They're not on the same level of not-human as the Created and Unchained are. The latter two are more akin to self-aware robots, while the former was born of humans and spent much of its life as a human before the Change.<br /> <br /> Mages claim to still be human, but, from a metagame stand point, they're &quot;Mental Monsters.&quot; I think its the same thing with werewolf, just in reverse. I see no reason for werewolves to be that different of a consideration from a changeling in this case. Especially given the wide variety of answers to the question of &quot;what happens when a vampire embraces a werewolf&quot; in popular culture.<br /> <br /> So, saying werewolves are automatically a no-go is kinda harsh, especially to me, since my personal pet theory is that vampires all originated as cannibalistic versions of other supernaturals. The prometheans that stole vitrol, human eating wolves, soul-stealing mages, shadow-eating fetches, and hungry ghosts all manage to thrive, but started to feed on each other. Over time, the whole &quot;you are what you eat&quot; rule came into play, and became more and more like each other, until we got the modern day vampires.<br /> <br /> So, Tremere, to me, aren't just vampire-like. They're beings who've started on the path to evolving into actual vampires.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the Werewolf books explicitly, both in terms of setting and mechanics, do not consider werewolves to be human, or at least no longer human. They are half-spirit beings. <br /> <br /> Similarly, mages are generally treated in all respects as human, although no longer subject to the Lie. They are like any other human with supernatural merits, although their abilities are significantly more versatile and powerful than virtually all other mortals. Conceptually, I've always compared Mage to the Dreden Files. Supernal Mages are akin to the very human and powerful White Council Wizards, feared and envied by the relatively numerous number other humans with lesser magical abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:18:43-07:00","id":467866,"title":"","content":"If they know about the Awakened. I imagine we'll all get a lot of interesting thoughts about that when the Orders are discussed in detail in Mage 2e.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every template has an easy to understand reason for why they wouldn't become Embraced, from the Awakened Soul to not actually being human at all. That said, if you wanna do it, go nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:26:19-07:00","id":467870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=467856#post467856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, mages are generally treated in all respects as human, although no longer subject to the Lie. They are like any other human with supernatural merits, although their abilities are significantly more versatile and powerful than virtually all other mortals. Conceptually, I've always compared Mage to the Dreden Files. Supernal Mages are akin to the very human and powerful White Council Wizards, feared and envied by the relatively numerous number other humans with lesser magical abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, the writers consider the Awakened to be &quot;monsters&quot;, but the most human monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:46:22-07:00","id":468034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=467856#post467856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the Werewolf books explicitly, both in terms of setting and mechanics, do not consider werewolves to be human, or at least no longer human. They are half-spirit beings.</div> </div> </div> </div> See, here's the thing. With the exception of hunters, none of the game lines are &quot;human&quot; by that standard. Like Saibot said, the writers have called the Awakened monsters as well. Mages may appear the most human, but they are, in fact, not. For a given value of &quot;human,&quot; that is. Remember, as well, that in-character voices (like the one nofather quoted) need to be taken with a grain of salt - they are what characters in the game tell themselves, not what is an objective fact from a game design stand point.<br /> <br /> However, all the PC splats (with two notable exceptions) start off as humans in one way or another. They had a human life before their transformation, they had a human soul that reacted like a human soul to soul damaging/stealing effects, they suffered as humans do to the Kiss, Lunacy, the Lie, and so on. <br /> <br /> This is completely different than Prometheans and Demons, both of whom have never been human. They don't have human souls, they have never had human souls, and human experiences are foreign to them. Trying to put werewolves on par with these alien minded beings is unfair, especially when a large part of the game's themes involves the balance between human flesh and wolf spirit. Trying to equate the three does a huge disservice to all three gamelines. My point was never &quot;werewolves are humans,&quot; it was that &quot;werewolves are just as much human as changelings are.&quot; Considering that changelings effectively transform into fae lords, that 'human' aspects are very much up to debate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, mages are generally treated in all respects as human, although no longer subject to the Lie. They are like any other human with supernatural merits, although their abilities are significantly more versatile and powerful than virtually all other mortals. Conceptually, I've always compared Mage to the Dreden Files. Supernal Mages are akin to the very human and powerful White Council Wizards, feared and envied by the relatively numerous number other humans with lesser magical abilities. </div> </div> </div> Mages are very much not humans with some powers. They are a different race of beings altogether. While physically, there's not a lot of change, spiritually, they are as different from a human as a vampire or werewolf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-03-2015, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:48:47-07:00","id":468038,"title":"","content":"You don't have to be a rock to be not human. There's a lot of room for things that aren't human between humans and animated statues.<br /> <br /> The human form is just a disguise for werewolves.<br /> <br /> But your nitpick was that werewolves 'claim' not to be human. But they aren't, and this is backed up repeatedly throughout the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2015, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:07:28-07:00","id":468296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=468038#post468038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But your nitpick was that werewolves 'claim' not to be human. But they aren't, and this is backed up repeatedly throughout the books.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its also undermined by ideas like Harmony that balances human flesh and wolf spirit. And my nitpick was that they are as much human as changelings are. That comparing them to alien beings that were never once human is wrong. &quot;They are like golems and robots, so no-go.&quot; That is what I was nitpicking. Its an objection to the extreme idea that werewolves are more inhuman than vamps, mages, changelings, and all other supernatural PCs.<br /> <br /> Werewolves also like to think of themselves as better, above the human herd. That mindset is reflected in the fiction, but its not a statement so inclusive to the point we can say &quot;No! They're not humans so no biting-embrace-shinanigans!&quot; Especially not when there are plenty of stories out there that contradict this. And not when we have to treat every other supernatural as individual cases.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't mortal humans, no. But they still have humanity inside of them. They were born human, and had a human soul for a good chunk of their life. In this way, they are just as human as one of the Sin-Eaters or Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-04-2015, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:42:08-07:00","id":468311,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it would be more accurate to say that werewolves are not <i>entirely</i> human. And not in the same way as sin eaters. Sin eaters are a fully human being bound to a separate, partially-ex-human entity.<br /> <br /> A werewolf is a human <i>and</i> a wolf spirit. And neither half is any less the &quot;real&quot; them than the other. In a way they were <i>always </i>not-quite-human. Their spirit half was dormant, weak enough to be destroyed if their human self was embraced or awakened or whatever but very much there. Now it is awake, and it is going nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:03:51-07:00","id":468349,"title":"","content":"Are Claimed human? Because that is the closest analog to the Uratha situation. They are half-human, half-wolf, half-flesh, half-spirit.<br /> <br /> On the Mage part, they are significantely less (or at least way different from) human in second edition even without accounting for magic. Now they change as they grow in knowledge with the Arcana Attainments. Even without a single spell on, a mage and a regular human are almost diferent species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:25:42-07:00","id":468355,"title":"","content":"Claimed can still separate, with enough effort. That's a major difference, and akin to the sin-eater situation. With werewolves, there's nothing to remove. It's all them. You can make a human and a spirit out of a claimed. You can't make a human and a spirit out of a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T08:35:29-07:00","id":468435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=467870#post467870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, the writers consider the Awakened to be &quot;monsters&quot;, but the most human monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Monster&quot; and &quot;human&quot; are certainly not mutually exclusive terms. Sadly, one needs to simply turn on the evening news to see how monstrous some human can be, often falling to a level of depravity and cruelty far in excess of a stereotypical vampire, werewolf or other strangeness.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I always felt that the Mage writers, at least in 1e, but now apparently even more so in 2e, believed that mages were in fact humans. This is emphasized in their Integrity analog that, unlike other templates, has the same breaking points as a regular humans, only with some additions relating to the &quot;wise&quot; use of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:41:34-07:00","id":468472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=468296#post468296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its also undermined by ideas like Harmony that balances human flesh and wolf spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually just flesh and spirit. They could just as easily be a wolf. Or a cat.<br /> <br /> Look no one's going to tell you what to do or not to do at your table. And if you want werewolves to be human there, that's great, if you want vampires to be able to Embrace them despite their not being human, that's great too. <br /> <br /> But people come to the forums for information. And stating again and again that werewolves are not human, despite the books and fans saying the opposite, is going to give people who come here for information the incorrect information. Can you at least appreciate that, outside of your own table, when the werewolf book says, 'Werewolves aren't human,' that, by the book, that's true?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-04-2015, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T12:50:21-07:00","id":468679,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's accept that they aren't human. <br /> <br /> However, they are less not human than Demons or Prometheans, in that they THOUGHT they were human for a long time. Same deal as far as I can tell with Beasts when they come out: they THOUGHT they were human, mostly (and couldn't put their finger quite on what was wrong with that idea) until they changed, and now they realize they were never human. <br /> <br /> BUT, and here's the important bit, up to that, their EXPERIENCE was as a HUMAN. They were experientally human, even if they were not technically, spiritually, scientifically, whatever human. That is what differs between Werewolves and Demons/Prometheans. <br /> Both are quite certainly Not Human. <br /> But Demons and Prometheans have also never been Experientially Human, while Werewolves have. Werewolves have gone through a period living as a human, in which for all intents and purposes they could have been human, but for the werewolf truth lying dormant in them. And that's what we're driving at here, is Experiental Humanity. <br /> <br /> Mummies are an interesting point here; they were definitely Human once, but they may not be Experientally Human anymore, as they may not have access to those experiences anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T12:54:26-07:00","id":468681,"title":"","content":"Their experience don't matter squat. Right now they are metaphysically as qualified for embrace as either of the two never-human splats. You'd be as fruitful trying to embrace a potato.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:43:33-07:00","id":468897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=468681#post468681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their experience don't matter squat. Right now they are metaphysically as qualified for embrace as either of the two never-human splats. You'd be as fruitful trying to embrace a potato.</div> </div> </div> </div>They qualify just as much as the mage, changeling, and sin-eater do. Technically, none of them are considered human enough to be Embraced, due to the no-cross-template-splatting rule. However, there's no reason for werewolves to be grouped with the never-humans, since, mechanically, they were human right up until the First Change.<br /> <br /> White room theorycraft time! Imagine a Mehket and a soon-to-be werewolf was sitting in a bar. The Mehket can get prophesy-like powers that could reveal that before the end of the night, the soon-to-be-wolf will become a full wolf and death rage, killing everyone in the room. The vampire decides to immediately embrace the werewolf potential before (s)he can turn.<br /> <br /> Now, ignoring the entire cheesiness of the situation, this would theoretically work. There's nothing about a soon-to-be-changed werewolf that would prevent them from being Embraced. So, at this point, they pretty much are humans. I don't think you can really get around that. The potential to become a werewolf doesn't make you not a human in terms of the Embrace. At no point does a Promethean (pre-New Dawn anyways) or Demon qualify.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Moving forwards - if we have a ST that throws that no-turning-into-another-tempalte rule out the window (which this entire discussion hinges on), then there's nothing about a werewolf that would make him disqualify from being Embraced. Especially in light of all the fiction out there that touches on the subject of hybrids, or the vamp curse destroying the ability to shapeshift. Demons and Prometheans wouldn't work, demons wouldn't work. There's nothing about a wolf that suggests they should be grouped with the alien minded machines. No more than any other supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:53:35-07:00","id":468905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=468897#post468897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They qualify just as much as the mage, changeling, and sin-eater do. Technically, none of them are considered human enough to be Embraced, due to the no-cross-template-splatting rule. However, there's no reason for werewolves to be grouped with the never-humans, since, mechanically, they were human right up until the First Change.<br /> <br /> White room theorycraft time! Imagine a Mehket and a soon-to-be werewolf was sitting in a bar. The Mehket can get prophesy-like powers that could reveal that before the end of the night, the soon-to-be-wolf will become a full wolf and death rage, killing everyone in the room. The vampire decides to immediately embrace the werewolf potential before (s)he can turn.<br /> <br /> Now, ignoring the entire cheesiness of the situation, this would theoretically work. There's nothing about a soon-to-be-changed werewolf that would prevent them from being Embraced. So, at this point, they pretty much are humans. I don't think you can really get around that. The potential to become a werewolf doesn't make you not a human in terms of the Embrace. At no point does a Promethean (pre-New Dawn anyways) or Demon qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>This situation would just beg me to say that the wolf First Change and murdering happens as a consequence to a near death experience (since Mekhet needs to kill him first) of being attacked (even if it's subtle biting) by the vampire. Just before his death, he goes First Change and starts bashing everybody around.... <br /> <br /> Other than this completely moot point, which ain't even a point to be raised here (just a funny thing I had to say), I have nothing to say...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:23:45-07:00","id":469036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=468679#post468679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT, and here's the important bit, up to that, their EXPERIENCE was as a HUMAN. They were experientally human, even if they were not technically, spiritually, scientifically, whatever human. That is what differs between Werewolves and Demons/Prometheans.<br /> Both are quite certainly Not Human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not made it through the rulebooks, but at least some Prometheans were made from human body parts. And in the fiction anthology, those that were have vague memories of their past lives. Presumably Embracing one of these humans before they could become part of a demiurge's make-a-human science project would work just as well as Embracing a wolf-blooded. Embracing a wolf-blooded, or one who may one day become a werewolf, opens a vampire up to the Dead Wolves bloodline.<br /> <br /> Demons, as well, can gain experiences through their cover. And according to at least one legend, a vampire did manage to Embrace an angel.<br /> <br /> But as I said before, you don't have to be a rock to be 'not human.' The souls of werewolves and sin-eaters are subourned by their spirit soul and geists respectively. Geister?<br /> <br /> Either way, being human isn't the sole factor in whether or not you can become a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-04-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T22:03:24-07:00","id":469173,"title":"","content":"Depending on the game I'm running. I'd go with: Templates are Equal so you can't write over them(So no embracing any major template). Templates are equal so you can write over them(Embrace a mage? Sure They lose their powers but they could Reawaken! Vampire gets dragged to Arcadia? HE's a changeling now!). Templates are weird-Trying to embrace a Template leads to odd circumstances that cannot be replicated and are generally bad.<br /> <br /> Which of these three I use depends on how central the game will to Embracing Supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T04:37:51-07:00","id":469284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=468905#post468905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This situation would just beg me to say that the wolf First Change and murdering happens as a consequence to a near death experience (since Mekhet needs to kill him first) of being attacked (even if it's subtle biting) by the vampire. Just before his death, he goes First Change and starts bashing everybody around....<br /> <br /> Other than this completely moot point, which ain't even a point to be raised here (just a funny thing I had to say), I have nothing to say...</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, in a real game, any good GM would laugh at this attempt. So much that could go wrong, with such potential plot fuel to run the game for months! It'd be like Christmas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:37:00-07:00","id":469577,"title":"","content":"I use the rule of suck to answer questions like this. Would it suck for a Promethean to be under a vampire's Vinculum? Probably. Ok, any critter capable of ingesting blood is susceptible to Vinculums. Ones with supernatural templates can resist with Willpower like vamps can. Would it suck for a blood-bonded mage to get free Disciplines? No. Ok, no combining ghouls with other templates.<br /> <br /> When in doubt, err towards whatever makes life more complicated for the characters involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T14:12:21-07:00","id":469592,"title":"","content":"I think that ones more down to &quot;you get <i>one</i> magic juice pool&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T23:27:48-07:00","id":469909,"title":"","content":"There's a Gangrel bloodline called Dead Wolves who were embraced before going through the First Change. They invented a discipline that lets them draw power from the moon similar to Werewolves, but that's the closest I've found to mixing templates.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also don't see why mages wouldn't be humans. They're born, they live, they can reproduce normally, and unless they go mad with power, they eventually age and die. The only thing different about them is they've awakened to the supernal realms and gain the benefits of an awakened existence. But they're still biologically human.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hardly see why becoming a vampire would have any impact on one's status as a mage. There are loads of bloodlines and even the covenants themselves have created their own forms of magic. Maybe a mage loses their connection to the supernal, but that doesn't mean they can't use magic anymore. If anything, their former existence might grant them the chance to develop entirely new disciplines!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-06-2015, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T23:55:14-07:00","id":469918,"title":"","content":"The Awakened Soul resists the Embrace, so they die and their corpses disappear, or something like that. I imagine that sort of pre-Embrace sorcery stuff is more the domain of other kinds of magic users, because the Awakened don't get Embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T00:04:01-07:00","id":469919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=469909#post469909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Gangrel bloodline called Dead Wolves who were embraced before going through the First Change. They invented a discipline that lets them draw power from the moon similar to Werewolves, but that's the closest I've found to mixing templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source?<br /> <br /> [quote]I also don't see why mages wouldn't be humans. They're born, they live, they can reproduce normally, and unless they go mad with power, they eventually age and die./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> So do dogs, apes, trees etc can't embrace them. Really the ability to Embrace something says a lot about its nature. I prefer to give my Mages some pause on the whole &quot;We are just normal humans with cool powers&quot; so them being unembraceable(or as Embraceable as anyone else) works to create a sense of dread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T04:49:55-07:00","id":470056,"title":"","content":"The Dead Wolves are in Shadows of Mexico.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T06:58:43-07:00","id":470103,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lian;n469919]<br /> <br /> Source?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't see why mages wouldn't be humans. They're born, they live, they can reproduce normally, and unless they go mad with power, they eventually age and die./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> So do dogs, apes, trees etc can't embrace them. Really the ability to Embrace something says a lot about its nature. I prefer to give my Mages some pause on the whole &quot;We are just normal humans with cool powers&quot; so them being unembraceable(or as Embraceable as anyone else) works to create a sense of dread. </div> </div> </div><br /> Their signature discipline is called Sublinario. It grants them special powers and abilities similar to those of werewolves, one of which improves their effectiveness at dealing with werewolves!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dead_Wolves\" target=\"_blank\">Dead Wolves</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-06-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T07:48:51-07:00","id":470120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;We are just normal humans with cool powers&quot; so them being unembraceable(or as Embraceable as anyone else) works to create a sense of dread. </div> </div> </div>I don't really see how that would work without going further into what the embrace actually is. On the face of it, the embrace is a pretty bad thing, a mage could pretty easily claim it just shows how broken most of humanity is that it can happen to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T13:56:39-07:00","id":470340,"title":"","content":"Well according to the Dead Wolves thing, it was possible to embrace someone with werewolf blood, but they lost the ability to become werewolves in the process of doing so. Maybe the &quot;immunity&quot; to the embrace means that they can not become vampires and retain their original powers? In the old world of darkness, the Tremere became vampires and lost their ability to use their original magical talents. They still became vampires, but they were no longer mages, at least not in the way they were before.<br /> <br /> I've read that in the nWoD, no mage or werewolf has ever been embraced, but the Ghost Wolves seem to suggest otherwise. Maybe they can be embraced, but lose what they previously were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:05:02-07:00","id":470343,"title":"","content":"As I recall, the Ghost Wolves are Wolfblooded, which isn't quite the same as being a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, in the 2nd Edition, getting turned into a major template (besides a werewolf obviously) doesn't necessarily remove a Wolfblooded's Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:12:17-07:00","id":470349,"title":"","content":"Dead Wolves. Ghost Wolves are tribeless werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:18:30-07:00","id":470354,"title":"","content":"Ascension magi and Masquerade Vampires were a bit different thematically. I mean, while Awakening at least makes the occasional suggestions that maybe being a mage isn't the greatest thing ever, Ascension didn't really bother, a mage is pretty much the exemplar of humanity. Likewise, Masquerade vampires combined vast potential power with a high degree of stasis; whereas Requiem vampries are highly adaptable (at least as of 2e), but don't have the same obvious paths to power.<br /> <br /> Ascension mage to Masquerade vampire had a genuine trade-off. You loose your dynamic vital soul for the potential to live forever (and maybe have a shot at being a 3rd gen god).<br /> That's still possible in NWoD but it's a bit less clearcut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:38:15-07:00","id":470367,"title":"","content":"Old WoD was way happier about splatmixing anyway. Abominations, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:20:36-07:00","id":470839,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is explicit mention of what can or can not be Embraced. However, the little relevant tidbits are &quot;mortal&quot; are Embraced and they lose their Integrity for Humanity. Werewolves, Mages, Changelings and everything else with a game line is not considered mortal, except Hunters so far, and none of those critters use Integrity, except Hunters. To throw all that under the bus, a Strix can combine with basically any corporeal humanoid to form a unique creature that presumably have qualities of a Strix, but not necessarily all the powers of the host (complicated). The Strix synthesis case isn't explained. It is just mentioned as a thing.<br /> <br /> I go by only humans, defined as anything using Integrity, can become something that doesn't use Integrity. A werewolf would have to die to be Embraced. A dead werewolf is a dead werewolf, not a dead human. That precludes werewolves from Embrace. Prometheans, Demons, Mages, Changelings, Mummies, Hosts, Claimed and anything I might have missed are in the same boat. Hunters can be Embraced. A Sin-Eater that is a possible candidate after the Geist part goes away.<br /> <br /> I believe the official position is as it has been. Once Integrity is replaced the replacement can only ever go back to Integrity, so going back to a mortal may be possible which would make further changes possible again. Prometheans can go mortal. Other beings <i>might</i> be able to go back to being a mortal. Nothing official on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T12:09:49-07:00","id":473183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463783-crossover-question?p=470343#post470343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, the Ghost Wolves are Wolfblooded, which isn't quite the same as being a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, in the 2nd Edition, getting turned into a major template (besides a werewolf obviously) doesn't necessarily remove a Wolfblooded's Tell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wolfblooded are people who have werewolf blood in them, but typically don't have enough to undergo the First Change. They have a resistance to Lunacy, and are usually stronger and more athletic than ordinary humans (pretty much the werewolf equivalent to a ghoul). They can even produce Werewolf offspring from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T13:57:36-07:00","id":473298,"title":"","content":"There's more to it as of 2e werewolf. Some of them are even werewolves by a broad definition (ie. a human who can turn into a wolf).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:24:56-07:00","id":473423,"title":"","content":"Wolf blooded can even be werewolves enough that a lot of fictional werewolves fit Wolf blooded better than they do full uratha: only able to take one other shape, not able to control it, that kinds thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:30:50-07:00","id":474399,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was thinking of Wolfblooded in 2e, hence Tells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}